  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The support facets of 3D finishing are now a `SupSet` (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/grid.rs`). A `SupSet` holds the facets and a uniform XY bucket grid in CSR layout (Ericson, \"Real-Time Collision Detection\", ch. 7).\n- These point scans read only the facets of the cell that holds the query point:\n  - `support_at`\n  - `support_grad`\n  - `ball_clear`\n  - `column_clear`\n  - `edge::fold_best`\n- Each scan keeps its own padded-box reject. Each cell lists its facets in ascending index, one time each. Thus the same f64 code runs on the same facets in the same order, and each answer has the same bits as the full scan.\n- The cell map is monotone. A facet whose padded box holds the point is always in the cell of the point.\n- The grid falls back to the full scan for a non-finite box, a non-finite query point, an extent that is not finite, more than `u32::MAX` facets, or an extent that no cell size fits. It never guesses a cell.\n- `SupSet::full_scan` keeps the old scan as the reference. The GPU filter of #2526 can compare against it.\n- Each `&[Sup]` parameter in `finishing3d` is now `&SupSet`. The loops that are not point queries read every facet, as before.\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2619-facet-grid.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nRelease build, parallel finishing, a height-field mesh, tool diameter 6, tolerance 0.01. One run each, with a temporary harness that is not committed.\n\n| Facets | Before | After | Output hash (before = after) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1800 | 13.161 s | 13.908 s | `a629dd9f259d227d` |\n| 7200 | 162.915 s | 161.515 s | `c719175f144437ae` |\n\nThe grid gives no measurable gain on this job. The point scans are not the hot path here. The output is the same. A profile must find the hot path before more speed work.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nLib unit tests in `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/grid_tests.rs`. The scan functions are `pub(super)`, so a file in `crates/motion/tests/` cannot reach them.\n\n- `grid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_bumps`: tool radius 0.4, 0.5, 1 and 3 against cell 1, 0.37, 5 and the automatic size. Boxes on cell borders, and a tool larger than a cell.\n- `grid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_big_and_degenerate_facets`: facets larger than many cells, a steep wall, zero-area facets (one point, a repeated vertex, a collinear facet).\n- `grid_candidates_hold_every_facet_whose_box_holds_the_point`: the superset law, the order and no duplicates.\n- `non_finite_input_falls_back_to_the_full_scan`: NaN and infinite vertices, non-finite query points, an empty set.\n\nThe parity tests compare the bits of `support_at`, `support_grad`, `fold_best`, `plunge_support`, `ball_clear` and `column_clear` between the grid and the full scan. A test mutation (a miss of 2% of a cell at the upper edge) makes two tests fail.\n\nQuick gate on `2eefe69e5d6796e3bbfd35b4be5130b7dc7b767c`: 27 steps, 0 failed (motion lib and the finish3d suites, app `golden_cl` and `operations` included). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. No golden `.cl` or `.nc` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The release lanes and the large-fixture golden runs (`#[ignore]`).\n- Parallel raster lines (the optional item of the issue). Not done.\n- The speed on the real part models. The readings come from one synthetic mesh.\n\nChangelog: 3D finishing: the drop-cutter support scan uses a facet grid; the toolpaths do not change.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2619\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
